;; spec:   stdlib §2.5 (a bulk vec builds the trie in one pass), §8.1 item 5 (count cases)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 150
;; audit:  clean
;; allocs: <= 21
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: vec
;; vec of an Array of 150 elements, the walk's default to-vec: 4 full leaves and 22 elements in the buffer,
;; so the leaves array (made with 4 slots when the first leaf is full) has not yet had to double (its
;; doubling is the 5th leaf, the 161st element, and costs 4 objects: 25 at 161). A leaves array that
;; starts smaller doubles earlier (2 more objects here: 23), and one that starts larger is not filled
;; when the walk ends, so the root branch is a copy of it and not the array itself (1 more: 22); every
;; element still reads right either way, so only the count shows it. The mutation review (MUT-L9)
;; found `(array 4 leaf)` to `(array 3 leaf)` and to `(array 5 leaf)` surviving every case before this
;; one. 21 is measured; the harness's own test lowers the bound by one and requires the failure.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((v (vec (array 150 0))))
    (count v)))
